title: Banking Crisis
subtitle: The collapse of the German banking system...
new-page: true
on-arrival: banking_crisis_seen = 1; workers_kpd += 5; workers_nsdap += 3; new_middle_nsdap += 3; old_middle_nsdap += 4; rural_nsdap += 3; unemployed += 3; crisis_urgency += 1; workers_spd -= 4 if spd_in_government; new_middle_spd -= 5 if spd_in_government; old_middle_spd -= 5 if spd_in_government; rural_spd -= 4 if spd_in_government; economic_growth -= 1;
tags: event
view-if: customs_union = 1 and banking_crisis_timer = 0
max-visits: 1
face-image: img/danat_bank.jpg

= Banking Crisis

The Darmstädter und Nationalbank, or Danat Bank, has collapsed! Along with it goes much of the German banking system. The cause seemed to be due to the government's pursuit of a customs union with Austria, which led to de facto international sanctions.

This is a bourgeois dispute, but the costs will be borne by the proletariat. The people are facing ever-increasing hunger and poverty, and perhaps we are partly to blame.

- @nationalize: Take over the Danat Bank!
- @nothing_to_do: There is nothing we can do.
- @stabilization: Take action to stabilize the economy!
- @austerity: Chancellor [+ chancellor +]'s response is, as always, more austerity.
- @end_toleration: We are tired of austerity. End the toleration arrangement!

@nationalize
view-if: spd_centrist and spd_in_government
choose-if: (economic_minister = "Naphtali" and economic_democracy >= 4) and not dvp_in_government
unavailable-subtitle: [? if not economic_minister = "Naphtali": Naphtali could be useful here. ?] [? if economic_democracy < 4: Lower level control of economy is insufficient to even initiate this action. This requires **economical democracy**. ?] [? if dvp_in_government: DVP would not let this happen ever. ?]
subtitle: The very first step of **Organized Capitalism**.
on-arrival: budget += 1; danat_nationalized = 1; workers_spd += 5; socialism += 5; unemployed -= 1; economic_growth += 2; dvp_relation -= 5; capital_strike_progress += 2; inflation += 1.5; ddp_relation -= 3; z_relation -= 4

According to our economist Rudolf Hilferding, this failing project is best to be nationalized, so government could control the part of economy much more efficiently. Although our bourgeouis partners disagree with us, they can't do much in the face of collapse of bank and it's value. Thus, bank has been nationalized, reducing the influence of private sector.

@nothing_to_do
view-if: spd_in_government = 1
on-arrival: welfare -= 1; workers_spd -= 3; unemployed_spd -= 3; pro_republic -= 3

There is, essentially, nothing we can do.

@stabilization
view-if: spd_in_government = 1
subtitle: -1 budget
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: workers_spd += 3*(1-dissent); new_middle_spd += 3*(1-dissent); old_middle_spd += 2*(1-dissent); rural_spd += 2*(1-dissent); unemployed -= 2; inflation += 1 if inflation < 0; budget -= 1; workers_nsdap -= 3; economic_growth += 0.9;

In the face of the banking crisis, we have taken emergency action to stabilize the economy by injecting money into the banking system. It might not be enough, but it temporarily staunches the bleeding.

@austerity
view-if: spd_in_government = 0
on-arrival: welfare -= 1; workers_spd -= 3; unemployed_spd -= 3; pro_republic -= 3; economic_growth -= 1;

Chancellor [+ chancellor +] responds to the banking crisis with more cuts to welfare.

@end_toleration
view-if: spd_toleration = 1
on-arrival: time_to_election = 3; spd_in_government = 0; in_grand_coalition = 0; spd_toleration = 0;
call: set_next_election_time

We are tired of [+ chancellor +]'s policy of austerity. After [+ chancellor +]'s attempt to use emergency powers to pass another welfare cut, we have worked with the other parties to reverse this policy. In response, the Reichstag has been dissolved, and new elections called.

New elections have been set for [+ next_election_month : month +] [+ next_election_year +].
